<title>USA: Dillard files for $400 mln debt offering.</title>
<headline>Dillard files for $400 mln debt offering.</headline>
<dateline>WASHINGTON 1997-05-01</dateline>
<text>
<p>Dillard Department Stores Inc on Thursday filed with the U.S. Securities and Exchange Commission for a shelf offering of up to $400 million in debt securities.</p>
<p>When combined with previously registered debt, the offering totals $500 million, the Little Rock, Ark, department store chain said.</p>
<p>The company said it would use the proceeds for general corporate purposes.</p>
<p>No underwriters were named in the filing.</p>
</text>
